B.eII=new A.y("Movement","The muscles at the back of your thigh that bend your knee when you run.")
B.f2G=new A.y("Movement","The calf muscle pushes you up on your toes when you walk, run and jump.")
B.f3N=new A.y("Movement","These lift your foot up so your toes do not drag on the ground.")
B.eXo=new A.y("Nerves","Weighs about 1.4 kg and uses a fifth of your energy. It has around 86 billion nerve cells and runs everything you do.")
B.f2V=new A.y("Hormones","A butterfly-shaped gland in your neck. It makes hormones that control how fast your body uses energy.")
B.eJY=new A.y("Breathing","The trachea carries air down to your lungs. Rings of tough cartilage keep it open.")
B.f4q=new A.y("Digestion","The oesophagus squeezes food down to your stomach in waves, so you can swallow even upside down.")
B.eO0=new A.y("Breathing","You breathe about 20,000 times a day. Spread flat, your lungs would cover a tennis court.")
B.f23=new A.y("Blood","About the size of your fist. It beats around 100,000 times a day and pumps blood round a track 100,000 km long.")
B.eRn=new A.y("Breathing","A dome-shaped muscle under your lungs. It pulls down to suck air in. A hiccup is it twitching.")
B.eV8=new A.y("Digestion","Cleans your blood and stores energy. It is the only organ that can grow back after damage.")
B.f_r=new A.y("Digestion","A small green pouch that stores bile, a juice that helps you digest fatty food.")
B.f4A=new A.y("Digestion","Acid in your stomach could dissolve metal, but a thick layer of mucus protects it.")
B.f4s=new A.y("Blood","Filters old blood cells and helps fight germs. You can live without it.")
B.f4w=new A.y("Digestion","Makes juices to digest food and insulin, a hormone that controls the sugar in your blood.")
B.eVH=new A.y("Cleaning","Clean about 180 litres of blood every day and turn the waste into urine.")
B.f0m=new A.y("Digestion","About 6 metres long, folded up in your tummy. This is where most food is turned into energy for your blood.")
